  "development_scheme": "Leave-one-month-out over all twelve months of 2025 for the residual stage. For a held-out month every variant is fitted on the in-scope rows of the other eleven months (scratch/v24 frames: cross-fit v9 on clock-present rows, the provenance that ships; the label-free matches_v11 feature caches of adsb_v24) and predicts the held-out month. Reading 1 (all twelve months): the residual stage's own out-of-sample RMSE on its scope (matched non-LIRF rows, v9 + r against the label), pooled over the twelve months by rows. Reading 2 (the four recipe months, the only months with out-of-sample committee tables): every candidate is built with the frozen blend arithmetic (tools/run_adsb_v11.candidate_values) and scored on ALL rows (every label, no clipping) against the incumbent's development prediction, which the tool must reproduce exactly from runs/adsb_v24/dev/predictions_<month>.parquet. The blend tables are the incumbent's out-of-sample fold predictions (January / July / November) and the cached January-November refit leaves (December), identical for baseline and candidates. The eight other months score the residual stage only.",
